🔢 Distinct Count Across Totals in Power BI (DAX Patterns)
🧠 Overview

When building a Matrix in Power BI with Year, Quarter, and unique product counts, the default behavior is misleading:

Quarter counts are correct.

But the Total row simply adds quarter counts together, even if products overlap.

This guide shows how to fix Matrix totals by creating a summarized table so the total row reflects the true distinct count across all quarters.

📊 Use Cases

Count unique products per quarter and per year correctly.

Ensure total row = true distinct count, not a sum of distinct counts.

Use DAX patterns for scenarios where totals don’t behave as expected in matrices.

